<article class="ws-sheet">
<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; History by century</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: The 3rd century</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on the 200s: the states, events and people of the century. Use its page to find the answers.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/centuries/3rd-century">Open the century page &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><p class="ws-how">Each number marks the capital or seat of a state that existed in 250 CE. Write its name from the word bank on the line with the same number.</p><figure class="ws-mapfig"><svg class="map map-world ws-map" viewBox="0 0 10711 5638" role="img" aria-label="Map: 8 numbered states of the world in 250 CE"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><g class="ws-pins"><g><circle cx="5304" cy="942" r="182"/><text x="5304" y="1018" font-size="219">1</text></g><g><circle cx="2331" cy="1704" r="182"/><text x="2331" y="1781" font-size="219">2</text></g><g><circle cx="5772" cy="1297" r="182"/><text x="5772" y="1373" font-size="219">3</text></g><g><circle cx="6757" cy="1168" r="182"/><text x="6757" y="1245" font-size="219">4</text></g><g><circle cx="6060" cy="1908" r="182"/><text x="6060" y="1984" font-size="219">5</text></g><g><circle cx="8115" cy="1035" r="182"/><text x="8115" y="1111" font-size="219">6</text></g><g><circle cx="6152" cy="991" r="182"/><text x="6152" y="1067" font-size="219">7</text></g><g><circle cx="4821" cy="1043" r="182"/><text x="4821" y="1119" font-size="219">8</text></g></g></svg><figcaption>The world in 250 CE</figcaption></figure><p class="ws-bank"><b>Word bank:</b> Roman Egypt &middot; Goguryeo &middot; Aksumite Empire &middot; Lusitania &middot; Kushan Empire &middot; Caucasian Albania &middot; Teotihuacan &middot; Roman Empire</p><ol class="ws-blanks"><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li></ol></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the events from 1 (earliest) to 6 (latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Xiaoting</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Hormozdgan</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Red Cliffs</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Crisis of the Third Century</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Edessa</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Constitutio Antoniniana</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right dates next to each person. Look them up in the encyclopedia.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Caracalla</li><li>Cyprian</li><li>Cassius Dio</li><li>Cao Pi</li><li>Gallienus</li><li>Constantius I</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>188–217</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>187–226 CE</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 218–268</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 210–258</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 250–306</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 165–c. 235</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Key terms</h2><p class="ws-how">These words appear in the entries of this century. Explain each one in your own words.</p><ul class="ws-terms"><li><b>Latin</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>Piracy</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">5</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>In the 200s, 41 recorded states were founded and 62 came to an end. Choose one of each from the century page. What happened to them?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The great powers of the age included the Roman Empire, the Teotihuacan and the Africa Proconsularis. Choose one: what made it strong in these hundred years, and what threatened it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose one event from the list and one person. How might they be connected? Use the encyclopedia to find out.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>If you could visit one place in the 3rd century, where would you go, and what would you hope to see?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/centuries/3rd-century. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: The 3rd century</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Roman Empire <span>27 BCE – 476 CE</span></li><li>Teotihuacan <span>100 BCE – 550 CE</span></li><li>Roman Egypt <span>30 BCE – 641 CE</span></li><li>Kushan Empire <span>30 CE – 375 CE</span></li><li>Aksumite Empire <span>100 CE – 940 CE</span></li><li>Goguryeo <span>37 BCE – 668 CE</span></li><li>Caucasian Albania <span>100 BCE – 510 CE</span></li><li>Lusitania <span>27 BCE – 439 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Battle of Red Cliffs <span>208</span></li><li>Constitutio Antoniniana <span>212 CE</span></li><li>Battle of Xiaoting <span>221–222</span></li><li>Battle of Hormozdgan <span>224 CE</span></li><li>Crisis of the Third Century <span>235–284 CE</span></li><li>Battle of Edessa <span>260 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Caracalla <span>1: 188–217</span></li><li>Cyprian <span>4: c. 210–258</span></li><li>Cassius Dio <span>6: c. 165–c. 235</span></li><li>Cao Pi <span>2: 187–226 CE</span></li><li>Gallienus <span>3: c. 218–268</span></li><li>Constantius I <span>5: c. 250–306</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Key terms</h2><dl class="ws-key-terms"><dt>Latin</dt><dd>Latin is the language of ancient Rome, which spread across the western Mediterranean with Roman rule and became the root of the Romance languages.</dd><dt>Piracy</dt><dd>Piracy is robbery and violence committed at sea.</dd></dl></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">5</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers name states, people and events from the century page.</p></section></div></details>
